Request by book: https://github.com/Getty/p5-git-native/issues/2 — there is no way to reach libgit2's git_object_id_from_buffer (https://libgit2.org/docs/reference/main/object/git_object_id_from_buffer.html) through Git::Native. Done: a documented, tested API that hashes a Perl buffer as blob/tree/commit/tag and returns the oid, matching git hash-object.

Done in c6ea511 on gh-issue-2. Decision: Oid->from_buffer(bytes, type) via git_odb_hash (older, universal; object_id_from_buffer needs newer libgit2). Wide chars and bad type croak.
